; Fellowship.rfl exports, in the order and spelling the retail engine uses.
;
; All eleven are undecorated, which means the originals are extern "C" __cdecl.
; The names must match exactly: the host resolves them by GetProcAddress, so a
; typo here is not a link error, it is a silent "RFL initialization fail" at
; runtime with nothing to say which one was missing.
;
; Ordinals are pinned to the retail values. Nothing observed so far imports by
; ordinal, but a host that did would break invisibly if these drifted.
;
; No LIBRARY directive: it writes the module name into the export table, and
; since this DLL is built as Fellowship.rfl rather than Fellowship.dll the
; linker would warn that the two disagree and then ignore it anyway.
;
; DllMain is exported because the retail module exports it. Nothing is known to
; call it by name, but a drop-in replacement that quietly offers fewer symbols
; than the thing it replaces is a trap for whoever debugs it next.
EXPORTS
    GetBaseRFLInterface     @1
    GetLandTypeInterface    @2
    GetMessageInterface     @3
    GetObjTypeInterface     @4
    GetObjectDefInterface   @5
    IsObjectLight           @6
    IsObjectMoveNode        @7
    IsObjectPortal          @8
    RiotDllGetID            @9
    RiotDllType             @10
    DllMain                 @11
